 "notes": "landA8 landscape-only pass (buildings/walls skipped). Views: Yandex z18 overview + z19 close views (NW institution, SW school sports/construction lot, E L-building yard, SE canal/bridge, NE service yard), all features cross-checked on the z18 overview. Institution with green roofs (x~194-282,y~580-660): light paved yard N of it, 6-7 m paved strip along its W side (model has lawn/building there), paved inner courtyards; a paved lane (footpath 4 m) joins the strip to the end of the school access road at (237.7,572.2). School cluster S of it: artificial-turf pitch (sport/turf, x~187-223,y~526-544; model sport pitch is ~6 m further W), dark-green hard court N of it with 2 white objects (sport/rubber, uncertain type), red-brown rubber play surface (playground/rubber, no equipment visible, trees on it), blue court (sport), paved forecourt (plaza), basketball court (sport/asphalt) which the model marks as playground (x~289-307,y~540-554). Model playgrounds NOT confirmed: under tree canopy W of institution (x~159-191,y~583-670), in private-house gardens NW of the pitch (x~160-191,y~551-597), and the fenced grass square in the service yard N of the L-shaped building (x~374-391,y~700-722, grass, no equipment - excluded from the yard polygons). Parking only where cars stand: 3 cars along front of N building (x~160-186,y~712-717), 3 cars nose-in S of the E-W street (x~290-307,y~502-513), 4 cars nose-in on S side of E street (x~427-445,y~535-541). Soil: large bare-earth construction lot around the unfinished building in the SW (clipped at y=450), bare lot E of the L-building asphalt yard, walled vacant plot W of the canal street, bare ground with young trees S of the NE E-W street. Alley: lane (6 m) between the N building row and garages linking the street bend at (203,702) to the dead end of the canal-side street at (251.7,695.6). Note for building pass: the long L-shaped grey-roof building (x~354-376,y~593-676) is missing from the model footprints. No other visible footpaths (yards between houses are under canopy)."
